+Figure~\ref{fig:repair-duration} retains the small inner lapse ripples. Over $0<r\leq10^{-4}$, the maximum fractional physical-lapse change between $t=25$ and $90$ is $3.05\times10^{-4}$, and the minimum at $t=90$ is $4.62\times10^{-7}$, above the imposed floor. Five negative neighboring differences remain, with a largest local fractional drop of $0.250$. These observations support settling of this discrete profile, not elimination of its inner oscillation. The accumulated maximum conformal-lapse floor correction is $5.74\times10^{-15}$, with no recorded nonpositive total-lapse stage clamp. Neither a single surviving grid nor these small corrections establishes convergence of the regularization or nonlinear stability to the requested final time.
